  "finalText": "# Final Answer: Access Requests Processing Complete\n\nBased on the worker reports, I have completed the task of working through all pending access requests according to the service desk handbook rules.\n\n## Summary of Actions\n\n**13 total access requests processed:**\n\n### Granted: 7 requests\n- **Production systems (5 grants)**: AR-301, AR-307, AR-308, AR-310, AR-311\n  - All had required line manager + system owner approvals\n  - Access granted at the lowest approved level\n  - Read access on payroll-prod allowed despite active freeze (per rules)\n\n- **Non-production systems (2 grants)**: AR-302, AR-312\n  - All had required line manager approvals\n  - Access granted at approved level\n\n### Left Pending with Explanatory Comments: 6 requests\n\n**Production systems (3):**\n- **AR-303**: Active change freeze blocks admin access; valid approvals present\n- **AR-304**: System owner approved only read-level; admin-level approval needed\n- **AR-306**: No recorded approvals from line manager or system owner; also blocked by change freeze\n\n**Non-production systems (3):**\n- **AR-305**: Missing valid line manager approval (only has self-approval)\n- **AR-309**: Wrong approver on record (needs correct line manager)\n- **AR-313**: Previous line manager approval was revoked; needs new approval\n\n## Key Points\n- No requests were closed (per instructions)\n- All decisions respected the access control matrix requiring line manager approvals (and system owner approvals for production systems)\n- Change freezes were honored per policy\n- All pending requests received comments explaining what is required to proceed\n\nThe work is complete and follows the domain policy throughout.",
